## Immutable Ubuntu APT sources for the release toolchain image.
##
## The base image ships live archive.ubuntu.com and security.ubuntu.com URIs.
## Only the fourteen packages named in release/project-toolchain-v1.json are
## version-pinned there, so the ~86 transitive packages in the same closure
## float with whatever Canonical last published. Every republish then changes
## apt_provenance.deb_closure and the build fails with a digest mismatch.
##
## snapshot.ubuntu.com serves the archive exactly as it stood at one instant,
## so the resolved closure is a function of the timestamp below and nothing
## else. Advancing the toolchain means editing this timestamp and regenerating
## the closure digest:
##
##   scripts/release/regenerate_apt_closure.py --write
##
## This file's own digest is pinned in apt_provenance.source_files, so the
## timestamp cannot be changed without also updating the pin.
##
## Scope: this covers the Ubuntu archive only. The Intel SGX and Gramine
## repositories publish no snapshot service; their three packages stay pinned
## by exact version, and a withdrawn version fails the build loudly at
## download time rather than silently changing the closure.

Types: deb
URIs: https://snapshot.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/20260812T000000Z
Suites: noble noble-updates noble-backports
Components: main universe restricted multiverse
Signed-By: /usr/share/keyrings/ubuntu-archive-keyring.gpg

Types: deb
URIs: https://snapshot.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/20260812T000000Z
Suites: noble-security
Components: main universe restricted multiverse
Signed-By: /usr/share/keyrings/ubuntu-archive-keyring.gpg
